  1179, 2028, ARRAY[0.0,0.01,0.017,0.027,0.032,0.037,0.042,0.037,0.04,0.043,0.046,0.093,0.158,0.202,0.254,0.293,0.35,0.372,0.411,0.463,0.493,0.537,0.576,0.594,0.602,0.606,0.586,0.573,0.592,0.625,0.66,0.717,0.738,0.775,0.815,0.866,0.903,0.956,0.974,1.0]::numeric[], $nm$2028 M$nm$, $nm$A long climb from the village of Shybene, at about 850 m, to Pip Ivan Chornohirskyi (2,028 m) in the Chornohora range — 11 km and 1,180 m of ascent. The first 700 m are on a minor road, then a track and path take over; OpenStreetMap rates the trail as mountain hiking (SAC T2). Along the way a spring and camp spots are mapped near Maricheyka (1,510 m) and further up. Plan a full day.

