values ('2debeb9d-7475-573a-8cf7-e45955d8e78f', 'ddad1e11-32c5-529e-9c8e-937caed5d76b', $nm$Petros ridge
Lazeshchyna to Yasinia$nm$, $nm$CHORNOHORA, UKRAINE$nm$, $nm$https://smdnbjvelqsgjoubognc.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/route-covers/curated/petros-yasinia.jpg$nm$, 'hard', 'foot', $nm$FOOT$nm$, 33.25, $nm$48.2727° N, 24.4141° E$nm$, null, $nm$2 DAYS$nm$,
  1342, 2020, ARRAY[0.042,0.056,0.064,0.066,0.073,0.078,0.094,0.102,0.127,0.14,0.148,0.163,0.198,0.219,0.272,0.316,0.396,0.519,0.583,0.637,0.691,0.899,1.0,0.916,0.813,0.703,0.622,0.637,0.591,0.482,0.407,0.317,0.244,0.215,0.189,0.153,0.12,0.097,0.069,0.0]::numeric[], $nm$2020 M$nm$, $nm$A long traverse from Lazeshchyna to Yasinia over Petros (2,020 m), 33 km with 1,340 m of ascent — a full day or an overnight. About 10 km near the start are on a minor road, then tracks and footpaths climb to the ridge; OpenStreetMap tags part of the path as alpine hiking (SAC T4). Mapped along the way: Petros, Petrosul (1,848 m), several huts and camp spots, and one seasonal spring labelled as drying up, so carry water.

