values ('48a39146-6cc2-5b9d-93bd-ddd21d8c6b6b', 'ddad1e11-32c5-529e-9c8e-937caed5d76b', $nm$Rysy
from Palenica Białczańska$nm$, $nm$TATRAS, POLAND$nm$, $nm$https://smdnbjvelqsgjoubognc.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/route-covers/curated/rysy-palenica.jpg$nm$, 'hard', 'foot', $nm$FOOT$nm$, 12.3, $nm$49.2545° N, 20.1030° E$nm$, null, $nm$6 H$nm$,
  1532, 2499, ARRAY[0.0,0.009,0.017,0.037,0.049,0.06,0.068,0.082,0.095,0.076,0.079,0.1,0.128,0.125,0.134,0.165,0.2,0.215,0.22,0.23,0.253,0.262,0.279,0.286,0.289,0.291,0.278,0.278,0.281,0.324,0.388,0.415,0.405,0.426,0.509,0.612,0.7,0.821,0.911,1.0]::numeric[], $nm$2499 M$nm$, $nm$Rysy (2,499 m) from the Palenica Białczańska parking on the Polish side of the Tatras: 12.3 km and 1,530 m of ascent. The first 7.7 km follow the wide Droga Oswalda Balzera to Morskie Oko, then a footpath climbs past Czarny Staw and the Bula pod Rysami (2,055 m) to the summit. OpenStreetMap rates the upper section demanding alpine hiking (SAC T5): expect exposure and easy scrambling. Springs and the old PTTK hut at Morskie Oko are mapped along the way.

