values ('1ba2472e-28e8-55aa-8ea4-5ea8ba9ac960', 'ddad1e11-32c5-529e-9c8e-937caed5d76b', $nm$Adolf Munkel Weg
under the Odle$nm$, $nm$DOLOMITES, ITALY$nm$, $nm$https://smdnbjvelqsgjoubognc.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/route-covers/curated/odle-munkelweg.jpg$nm$, 'easy', 'foot', $nm$FOOT$nm$, 6.07, $nm$46.6252° N, 11.7806° E$nm$, null, $nm$2 H$nm$,
  352, 2047, ARRAY[0.066,0.155,0.202,0.27,0.262,0.31,0.357,0.426,0.601,0.643,0.506,0.464,0.472,0.523,0.596,0.559,0.528,0.617,0.681,0.829,0.814,0.552,0.404,0.197,0.029,0.0,0.097,0.231,0.406,0.39,0.494,0.559,0.597,0.685,0.685,0.667,0.736,0.905,0.949,1.0]::numeric[], $nm$2047 M$nm$, $nm$The Adolf Munkel Weg is an easy 6 km footpath that traverses beneath the Odle / Geisler rock walls in the Dolomites, between roughly 1,860 and 2,050 m, with only 350 m of total ascent. OpenStreetMap rates it mountain hiking (SAC T2) — no technical sections are tagged. A spring (Weißbrunn / Fontana Bianca) and the Brogleshütte hut (2,047 m) are mapped on the route.

