values ('2fdda331-4277-5f31-bfc1-5f04d5e01e90', 'ddad1e11-32c5-529e-9c8e-937caed5d76b', $nm$Alta Via 1
Fanes to Nuvolau$nm$, $nm$DOLOMITES, ITALY$nm$, $nm$https://smdnbjvelqsgjoubognc.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/route-covers/curated/av1-fanes-nuvolau.jpg$nm$, 'hard', 'foot', $nm$FOOT$nm$, 18.92, $nm$46.6120° N, 12.0142° E$nm$, null, $nm$7 H$nm$,
  1394, 2648, ARRAY[0.0,0.162,0.205,0.177,0.13,0.079,0.116,0.159,0.212,0.14,0.108,0.174,0.309,0.412,0.47,0.612,0.693,0.42,0.229,0.357,0.522,0.696,0.856,0.93,1.0,0.866,0.773,0.639,0.403,0.19,0.086,0.168,0.195,0.296,0.415,0.592,0.723,0.754,0.752,0.898]::numeric[], $nm$2648 M$nm$, $nm$A stage of Alta Via 1, the Dolomites long-distance trail from Lago di Braies to Belluno (about 120 km). This section runs 19 km from Rifugio Fanes (2,060 m) to Rifugio Nuvolau (2,574 m) via Rifugio Averau, climbing 1,390 m in total, with a high point near Averau (2,648 m). OpenStreetMap rates parts of it demanding mountain hiking (SAC T3) and one stretch follows the Sentiero del Fronte. Lech de Lagació, Lago de Limedes and other water points are mapped near the track.

