  132, 1035, ARRAY[0.891,0.819,0.853,0.952,0.884,0.727,0.648,0.676,0.621,0.573,0.509,0.509,0.549,0.396,0.379,0.348,0.232,0.372,0.379,0.451,0.549,0.536,0.369,0.287,0.188,0.239,0.41,0.58,0.672,0.652,0.809,0.867,0.99,1.0,0.829,0.621,0.71,0.775,0.334,0.0]::numeric[], $nm$1035 M$nm$, $nm$An 11 km section of the long trail around Makhtesh Ramon, the erosion crater in the Negev desert, from the Karne Ramon lookout to the Arod viewpoint. It follows footpaths and dirt tracks, passes Har Ramon (1,035 m) and the Borot Lots campsite, and has only 130 m of ascent. OpenStreetMap shows no drinking water within 150 m of this stretch, so carry everything you need.

