  1233, 831, ARRAY[0.0,0.124,0.268,0.487,0.392,0.523,0.685,0.636,0.671,0.762,0.736,0.862,0.887,1.0,0.893,0.927,0.963,0.984,0.97,0.92,0.882,0.922,0.941,0.974,0.966,0.973,0.938,0.989,0.896,0.857,0.824,0.793,0.75,0.667,0.69,0.628,0.793,0.633,0.618,0.633]::numeric[], $nm$831 M$nm$, $nm$Sprengisandsleið, road F26: 154 km across Iceland's central highlands, ranging between about 250 and 830 m. Almost the whole length is gravel; OpenStreetMap tags it as four-wheel-drive only and records a ford on the route. Camp and hut sites at Nýidalur and Versalir are mapped within 150 m of the track; plan fuel and supplies before you set out. Highland F-roads are mountain tracks, not ordinary roads.

