  533, 674, ARRAY[0.798,0.871,0.851,0.805,0.874,0.764,0.846,0.869,0.891,0.902,0.932,0.952,0.96,1.0,0.968,0.964,0.931,0.822,0.809,0.824,0.808,0.695,0.672,0.602,0.551,0.513,0.495,0.483,0.643,0.787,0.845,0.528,0.284,0.253,0.173,0.101,0.126,0.104,0.045,0.0]::numeric[], $nm$674 M$nm$, $nm$Kjalvegur, road 35 (the Kjölur route): 111 km through Iceland's interior between Langjökull and Hofsjökull, from about 210 m to 674 m. OpenStreetMap tags most of it as gravel (four-wheel-drive only), with a 15 km paved section at one end. An emergency hut and two viewpoints are mapped within 150 m of the track; services are far apart, so plan fuel and supplies in advance. Conditions change quickly in the highlands, so check local road reports before you go.

