values ('21a7b5cc-1531-5443-a9ad-39ba5f59eb10', 'ddad1e11-32c5-529e-9c8e-937caed5d76b', $nm$Danube–Moldau
cycle route$nm$, $nm$BAVARIAN FOREST, GERMANY$nm$, null, 'moderate', 'bike', $nm$BIKE$nm$, 63.98, $nm$48.8287° N, 13.7925° E$nm$, null, $nm$HALF DAY$nm$,
  670, 871, ARRAY[0.886,0.928,0.936,0.975,1.0,0.926,0.868,0.802,0.734,0.681,0.647,0.586,0.611,0.727,0.76,0.749,0.811,0.786,0.664,0.708,0.676,0.642,0.761,0.737,0.707,0.662,0.637,0.71,0.663,0.582,0.481,0.398,0.479,0.478,0.517,0.512,0.44,0.364,0.189,0.0]::numeric[], $nm$871 M$nm$, $nm$The Donau–Moldau cycle route runs 64 km from Haidmühle, by the Czech border, down through Neureichenau, Jandelsbrunn, Breitenberg and Wegscheid to Obernzell on the Danube, descending from about 870 m to 290 m. Half of it is on quiet minor roads, with cycle paths and short stretches of path between. The route is mostly gentle, with rolling climbs of about 670 m in total. Springs, a viewpoint at Braunberg (706 m) and a youth campsite at Rannasee are mapped near the track.

